#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120227 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efb9de21-feb6-5180-97c0-6a54b267864b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117863} {:answer/id #uuid "18aee910-e625-5d6b-8d45-7df9b301b29e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117864} {:answer/id #uuid "1eb13c80-7760-57a4-85cd-f9ba025fdc9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117865} {:answer/id #uuid "65324aa3-8e99-5930-8e14-9afcc5b14503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117866} {:answer/id #uuid "68e75bbe-b18e-5841-a327-16615239a361" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1eb13c80-7760-57a4-85cd-f9ba025fdc9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117865} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d8e254d-61d0-5a3a-b412-1448fa41d280" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117862}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "38bc27cb-fe0f-5096-8126-f66c64c344e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-34060" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-7 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 4 & 1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -15 \\\\ 4 & 1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 5 & k-28\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & k-28\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-3.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-3\\,⇒\\,k=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348064 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1885f6c6-1737-593d-a0b0-f40f204dfd3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348066} {:answer/id #uuid "d1920435-93cf-5231-beff-2dcd6353a8a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348067} {:answer/id #uuid "4824b77d-1f43-5121-ada6-096b6db97c87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348068} {:answer/id #uuid "646dfa8c-ad7c-5650-a692-9a13b2e1f363" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348069} {:answer/id #uuid "f6d5c801-e6e2-5bcb-bfe9-684cd229170a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1885f6c6-1737-593d-a0b0-f40f204dfd3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348066} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a9cffe4-2531-5e66-a9c8-2d9eb4d0f8e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2e640eb7-b1f9-5d7f-bab4-6d80d29a915a" :question/math-academy-id "q-34117" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, ${a}_{3}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+6{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-9 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 18 & -21 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-18{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+6{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+6(-1)=-4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+(-3){a}_{2}+(-1){a}_{3} & =b \\\\ 2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+(-3)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+(-1)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=2\\cdot (-3)\\cdot (-1)=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae44989b-7bf8-5c3e-bcb2-7a44520d1ff3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348073} {:answer/id #uuid "a908ed17-5d44-58f7-8b99-494b51e6e0a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348074} {:answer/id #uuid "873541a2-1bbb-5397-bc43-02cbfa9efd64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348075} {:answer/id #uuid "b0c2f712-5657-5e54-88da-49b70fb5dd7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348076} {:answer/id #uuid "ed587d61-4278-50c5-b0e5-2225f5d5a506" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed587d61-4278-50c5-b0e5-2225f5d5a506" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348077} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a7a6eaf-37f1-5d02-8771-868c922d65ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348072}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "23910d50-0ae0-541a-a349-4d3875b18617" :question/math-academy-id "q-74558" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\nk=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348078 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34998575-9291-54e0-93b5-fc74330599a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348080} {:answer/id #uuid "519a1a25-39cf-55ee-8354-8906ec4c3531" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348081} {:answer/id #uuid "e33cee3a-73ab-57e8-9bc9-394fe466daba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348082} {:answer/id #uuid "01819225-834d-52a6-af2c-8f870a7ff55f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348083} {:answer/id #uuid "29e4d8ee-9c40-5e68-bcb0-72cfd8dea909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29e4d8ee-9c40-5e68-bcb0-72cfd8dea909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348084} :answer-field/id #uuid "bac07c6a-6c30-5de7-9f62-812d75ad31cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348079}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "da2b75e4-b38a-5b5b-9891-19906308bd00" :question/math-academy-id "q-74600" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,4,-5⟩$, $c=⟨3,-9,15⟩$, and  $u=⟨2,-2,11⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s+3t=2 \\\\ 4s-9t=-2 \\\\ -5s+15t=11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -9 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 15 & 11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -5 & 15 & 11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=1,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $s$ and $t$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc=u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $u$ does *not* lie on the plane $Π.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348085 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63a484f0-484c-58b0-9efa-5029a2ac1698" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348087} {:answer/id #uuid "6ab9bb93-f976-5bef-a2fa-7f6edcfc54a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348088} {:answer/id #uuid "12f85f8b-8aa6-5a8d-95bb-bd83d6db6326" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348089} {:answer/id #uuid "a1d54eca-8daa-5b6d-94d9-17eba466f5e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348090} {:answer/id #uuid "79a0bf82-7dbc-56b7-96d5-180fc7911446" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ab9bb93-f976-5bef-a2fa-7f6edcfc54a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348088} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbf781fe-b8d3-5d9c-9dd6-1b0476a5ea24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348086}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "92084908-1bd4-5e88-bd7c-024c24724625" :question/math-academy-id "q-74602" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,7,-6⟩$, $c=⟨-2,-10,12⟩$, and  $u=⟨2,11,-12⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s-2t=2 \\\\ 7s-10t=11 \\\\ -6s+12t=-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 7 & -10 & 11 \\\\ -6 & 12 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 12 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s-2t=2 \\\\ 4t=-3 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n4t=-3\\,⟹\\,t=-\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s-2t & =2 \\\\ s-2(-\\frac{3}{4}) & =2 \\\\ s+\\frac{3}{2} & =2 \\\\ s & =2-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ s & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=\\frac{1}{2},\\,t=-\\frac{3}{4},$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{1}{2}b-\\frac{3}{4}c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{4})=-\\frac{3}{8}.$"}]}
